{
  "title": "85: al-Burooj البروج",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْبُرُوْجِۙ‏(1)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIL BOROOJE.\nBy the heaven full of Constellations!\nوَالْيَوْمِ الْمَوْعُوْدِۙ‏(2)\nWAL YAWMIL MAW-O’ODE.\nBy the Day promised!\nوَشَاهِدٍ وَّمَشْهُوْدٍؕ‏(3)\nWA SHAAHEDINW WA MASHHOOD.\nBy the witness and the witnessed!\nقُتِلَ اَصْحٰبُ الْاُخْدُوْدِۙ‏(4)\nQOTELA ASHAABUL UKHDOODIN.\nThat (Self) destroyed were the fellows of the ditch\nالنَّارِ ذَاتِ الْوَقُوْدِۙ‏(5)\nNAARE ZAATIL WAQOODE.\nOf the fire with fuel\nاِذْ هُمْ عَلَيْهَا قُعُوْدٌ ۙ‏(6)\nIZ HUM A’LAYHAA QO-O’ODUNW.\nWhen facing it sat they\nوَّهُمْ عَلٰى مَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ شُهُوْدٌ ؕ‏(7)\nWA HUM A’LAA MAA YAF-A’LOONA BIL-MOA-MENEENA SHO-HOOD.\nWhile they witnessed what they did unto the believers\nوَمَا نَقَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَمِيْدِۙ‏(8)\nWA MAA NAQAMOO MINHUM ILLAA AN-Y YOA-MENOO BIL-LAAHIL A’ZEEZIL HAMEEDIL.\nThey tormented (them) for naught but that they believe in God, the Ever-Prevalent, the Most Praised\nالَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ ؕ‏(9)\nLAZEE LAHOO MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZ, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEED.\nHe, unto Whom belongeth the Kingdom of the heavens and the earth; and God is, over all things, a Witness\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ فَتَنُوا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَتُوْبُوْا فَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ جَهَنَّمَ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ الْحَرِيْقِؕ‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA FATANUL MOA-MENEENA WAL MOAMENAATE SUMMA LAM YATOOBOO FALAHUM A’ZAABO JAHANNAMA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUL HAREEQ.\nVerily, those who persecute the believer men and the believer women, and yet they repent not, for them shall be the chastisement of the hell and for them is a burning torture\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ؕؔ ذٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْكَبِيْرُؕ‏(11)\nINNAL LAAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM JANNAATUN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAAR, ZAALEKAL FAWZUL KABEER.\nVerily, those who believe and do good deeds, for them shall be the gardens ‘neath which flow rivers; That shall be a great achievement\nاِنَّ بَطْشَ رَبِّكَ لَشَدِيْدٌ ؕ‏(12)\nINNA BATSHA RABBEKA LA-SHADEED.\nVerily the Grip of thy Lord is terrible\nاِنَّهٗ هُوَ يُبْدِئُ وَيُعِيْدُ‌ ۚ‏(13)\nINNAHU HOWA YUBDEO WA YO-E’ED.\nVerily, He it is Who originateth (everything) and causeth it to return\nوَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الْوَدُوْدُۙ‏(14)\nWA HOWAL GHAFOORUL WADOODO.\nHe is the Oft-Forgiver, the Most Loving One\nذُو الْعَرْشِ الْمَجِيْدُ ۙ‏(15)\nZUL A’RSHIL MAJEEDO.\nLord of the ‘Arsh ’ Glorious\nفَعَّالٌ لِّمَا يُرِيْدُ ؕ‏(16)\nFA’-A’ALUL LEMAA YOREED.\nThe Mighty Doer of whatsoever He willeth\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ الْجُنُوْدِۙ‏(17)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL JONOODE.\nHas not come unto thee the story of the hosts\nفِرْعَوْنَ وَثَمُوْدَؕ‏(18)\nFIR-A’WNA WA SAMOOD.\nOf Pharaoh and Thamood?\nبَلِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فِىْ تَكْذِيْبٍۙ‏(19)\nBALIL LAZEENA KAFAROO FEE TAKZEEBINW.\nNay! Those who disbelieve are (used) to belie\nوَّاللّٰهُ مِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ مُّحِيْطٌۚ‏(20)\nWAL LAAHO MINW WA-RAAA-EHIM MOHEET.\nWhile God is the Encompassing One, over them\nبَلْ هُوَ قُرْاٰنٌ مَّجِيْدٌ ۙ‏(21)\nBAL HOWA QURAANUM MAJEEDUN.\nNay! It is Qur’an the Glorious\nفِىْ لَوْحٍ مَّحْفُوْظٍ‏(22)\nFEE LAWHIM MAHFOOZ.\n(Inscribed) in the ‘Lauh al- Mahfuz’ (the Guarded Tablet)",
  "merits": "Surah al-Burooj (The Mansion Of Stars)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 22 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the one who recites this Surah will be near the Prophets and Messengers on the Day of Judgement. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of people who gather on the plains of Arafah.\nReciting this Surah saves one from dangers and if recited before sleeping, one is kept under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) for the whole night. When trying to wean a baby (stop it from breastfeeding and start eating solid foods), this Surah should be written and tied as a talisman around the baby’s neck."
